GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): the steady overworld's picture in between moves the world
exactly halfway, and 2D drawn over the scene is marked so it isn't slid with it.

- GPU3D: walking up or down the camera moves 1.5 pixels a scene (0.75 per world unit), and the
  picture in between moved the world back by half the scene's whole-pixel move (0 or 1), while
  the window slid it by the scene's own shift: the world showed 1.5, 0, 0.5 and 1 pixels a frame
  instead of 0.75 every frame (the user's play test, 2026-11-14: walking up stutters). Each scene
  now keeps where the world's origin lands before the shift (OrthoOrigin, kept through the swap),
  so the camera's true motion is known; the world is moved by the whole pixels nearest to
  halfway and the in-between's own shift (MidOrthoShift, shown as ShownOrthoShift for that frame)
  makes up the rest, at any speed. Anything moving on its own is moved by the whole pixels
  nearest to its own halfway (MidShift is in 1/256 pixel; patch 0022 uses fractions). Only when
  the scenes' overall motion matches the camera's; otherwise as before.
- GPU2D_Soft: Fixed2D, per main-engine line (Layer3D's columns), where a background or sprite is
  what shows, not alpha-blended with the 3D layer (BlendsWith3D, ColorComposite's decision).

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

